WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.003
-The President is lying
about former special counsel

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.105
Robert Mueller's
Congressional testimony.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.374
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:12.011
♪♪

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.747
Yesterday, the man who oversaw
a two-year investigation

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.216
into a criminal operation
by a foreign government

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.251
to interfere
in a presidential election

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:21.621
testified before Congress
on national television,

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:24.090
and right off the bat, he made
headlines when he said this.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.092
-Did you actually totally
exonerate the President?

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.394
-No.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.362
-Under Department of Justice
policy,

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.197
the President
could be prosecuted

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.133
for obstruction-of-justice
crimes after he leaves office.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.735
Is this correct?
-True.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.204
-Man, he was quick on the draw
with that answer.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.206
It's like he's been
waiting two years

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.108
for someone to ask him
that question.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.843
"And do you have
the handcuffs picked ou--"

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.245
"Yes!"

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.780
Over the course of seven hours,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.116
Mueller laid out details
of a criminal attempt

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.218
to interfere
in a presidential election,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.355
a campaign that openly welcomed
and encouraged that interference

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.523
in a series of lies
and potential attempts

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.759
to obstruct justice by
the President and his aides.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.162
In normal times, that
would be incredibly damning,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.696
and yet we're all
so numb to everything,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.665
people are acting like
because Mueller didn't come out

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.099
and say the words,
"Trump is guilty,"

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.501
it wasn't a big deal.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.002
But what were you expecting?

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:12.005
Did you think Mueller was
gonna smash through the wall

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:15.908
in a monster truck called
"The Detrumpulator"?

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.611
Mueller's report, in itself,
is already damning.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.347
We just got to see him
explain it on national TV.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.984
Yes, he occasionally stumbled
or had to consult the report,

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.087
but it's over 400 pages
with footnotes and citations.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.421
If you asked me under oath

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:31.991
about something I said
in "A Closer Look" yesterday,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.493
I'd have to consult
the script, too.

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:37.230
"Let's see.
I'd like to refer you

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.299
to appendix c, subsection 43b,

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.235
where in "A Closer Look"

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.170
we play the clip
of Elizabeth Warren

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.573
saying the words...
-Crazy [bleep].

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.908
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:52.912
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:56.582
Also...

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:59.385
it's pretty rich when the people
who complain that Mueller

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.121
stumbled over details
in a 400-page report

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:04.190
are the same people
who are totally fine

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.225
with Mr. Details over here.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:09.395
-This will be a plan where
you can choose your doctor.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.331
This will be a plan
where you can choose your plan.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:15.034
And you know what the plan is.
This is the plan.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:18.338
-I mean, it's very easy
not to stumble when you're just

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.307
using the same five words
over and over again.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.710
But give him something trickier,
like the word "lawmakers,"

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.112
and then see what happens.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.648
-He has worked
in both houses of Congress,

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:32.185
advising law-markers.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.487
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.823
-"The law-marker, of course.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.725
Being the Sharpie
that every judge uses

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:42.428
to write out
their legal decision.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:46.065
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.067
Thank you, law-marker."

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:51.838
Of course, Mueller's
very straightforward claim

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.773
that he could not exonerate
the President

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.676
comes after months of Trump
claiming unequivocally

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.044
that the Mueller Report

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.346
completely and totally
exonerated him.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.781
-There was no collusion
with Russia.

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:08.554
There was no obstruction
and none whatsoever.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:13.258
And it was a complete
and total exoneration.

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:15.828
-"No collusion, no obstruction.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.164
Complete and total exoneration.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.533
Keep America great."

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:26.039
-Total exoneration.
Complete vindication.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:29.007
-And, hey, you know, in this
case, you got to believe Trump

00:03:29.007 --> 00:03:31.410
because he definitely
read the report, right?

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.312
-I have not read
the Mueller Report.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:35.982
I haven't seen
the Mueller Report.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:39.719
As far as I'm concerned, I don't
care about the Mueller Report.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.654
-I mean, I'm not surprised
he didn't read it,

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.922
but it's jarring when he
just comes out and admits it.

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:47.193
He's like a guy at a book club
who's had a few glasses of wine

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:50.029
going, "But I guess
if I'm being totally honest,

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.830
my favorite part
of 'Fifty Shades of Grey'

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.767
was the cover,
because I did not read it.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.269
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:01.441
And, also, we are out of pinot!

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:05.111
By the way."

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.946
So, for four months,
Trump has been saying

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.048
the report completely
and totally exonerated him.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:12.251
How does he feel now
that Mueller said explicitly,

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.721
on national television,
that he did not exonerate Trump?

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:16.922
-There is no such a thing.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:20.193
He didn't have the right
to exonerate.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.594
And, you know,
it's very interesting.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.830
People mention exoneration.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.799
That was something
where he totally folded

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.101
because he never had
the right to exonerate.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.536
-Donald Trump has a tell.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:34.073
Whenever he goes, "You know,
it's very interesting..."

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:37.843
he's about to lay out
some five-star bull [bleep].

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:40.813
So Mueller made clear that
he could not exonerate Trump

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.715
because that was basically
his only option.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.717
Mueller couldn't just
straight-up indict Trump

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.519
because of Justice Department
guidelines

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.888
that say you can't indict
a sitting president.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.956
So instead,
he basically had to say,

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:53.091
"We can't exonerate
the president.

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:54.327
Now it's up to Congress."

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.362
But then Republicans
weirdly tried to claim

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.497
that Mueller that didn't have
the power to claim someone

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:00.733
was either exonerated
or not exonerated.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.000
One Republican Congressman

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.370
even made a big show
of that point using props,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.838
but Mueller wasn't having it.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.207
-Mr. Mueller,
does the attorney general

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.711
have the power or authority
to exonerate?

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.479
What I'm putting up here
is United States code.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.881
This is where the attorney
general gets his power

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:19.151
in the Constitution and
the annotated cases of these,

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.586
which we've searched.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.755
We even went to your law school,
'cause I went to Case Western,

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.158
but I thought maybe your law
school teaches it differently.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:28.695
And we got the criminal-law
textbook from your law school.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.997
Mr. Mueller, nowhere in these,
'cause we had them scanned,

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:35.268
is there a process or
description on exonerate.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.635
There's no office of exoneration

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:38.204
at the attorney general's
office.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.473
There's no certificate
at the bottom of his desk.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.208
Mr. Mueller,
would you agree with me

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:47.379
that the attorney general does
not have the power to exonerate?

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.882
-Uh, I'm going to pass on that.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.516
-[ Chuckles ] Oh.
It's such a bummer

00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:53.051
when you bust out
all your books,

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:55.588
and the other guy doesn't care.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:58.291
I feel so bad for the staff
that had to get all that stuff.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.192
I feel like this isn't
gonna work out

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:01.527
the way you think it will.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.895
"Oh, trust me!

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.698
When he sees the books,
his head will explode!"

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.533
I'm gonna be like,

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:11.137
"Do you remember this one
from your law school?!"

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.706
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.774
Of course,
no matter what Mueller said,

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:18.511
nothing was going to stop Trump
from declaring victory,

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:21.180
which is what he did on his way
to an event last night

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.950
in West Virginia, when he
once again stopped by reporters

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:27.386
for his usual chopper-adjacent
Q and Yell.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.054
-There was no defense

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.890
of what Robert Mueller
was trying to defend,

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.059
in all fairness
to Robert Mueller,

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:37.763
whether his performance
was a bad one or good one.

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.732
I think everybody
understands that.

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:43.102
I think everybody understands
what's going on.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:48.474
This has been a very bad thing
for our country.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.509
And despite everything
we've been through,

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:53.378
it's been an incredible
2 1/2 years for our country --

00:06:53.378 --> 00:06:57.182
the administration,
our president -- me.

00:06:57.182 --> 00:07:00.386
-Oh, you! You're the president!

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.221
Well...

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:05.090
That explains a lot.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.960
Later, Trump was asked
about Mueller's assertion

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.963
that Trump's aides had lied
during the investigation,

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.533
and Trump both denied
that Mueller had said that

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:16.502
and also claimed
the reporter herself was lying

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.970
by asking the question.

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.410
-Let me just tell you something.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.245
I know
You always have a question.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:31.417
You mean my
White House aides lie?

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:35.154
What about his aides?
What about Mueller's aides?

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.493
He didn't say that at all.

00:07:41.493 --> 00:07:43.528
You're untruthful
when you ask --

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:46.598
You are untruthful
when you ask that question.

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:49.035
When you ask that question,
you're untruthful.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:51.270
And you know
who else is untruthful?

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.273
You know who else is untruthful?
His aides.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:58.343
-Why does anyone even
ask him questions anymore?

00:07:58.343 --> 00:08:02.114
It's like continuing to put
dollar bills in a jukebox

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.949
that only plays
"Achy Breaky Heart"

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.618
no matter
what buttons you press.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.386
Also, can we go back to this?

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:14.026
-Let me just tell you something.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.928
I know.
You always have a question.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.896
-Yeah.
She always has a question.

00:08:17.896 --> 00:08:20.399
She's a reporter!

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.567
When the mailman shows up
at your door, do you say,

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:25.137
"Oh, let me guess. An envelope?

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:26.705
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:29.875
Would a pizza kill you,
mailman?"

00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:32.612
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:36.014
Mueller was also asked yesterday
about Trump's various attacks

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:39.084
on his investigation,
and his answers were very clear.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:41.654
-When Donald Trump called
your investigation a witch hunt,

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:43.556
that was also false, was it not?

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.157
-I'd like to think so, yes.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.993
-Well, your investigation
is not a witch hunt, is it?

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:49.394
-It is not a witch hunt.

00:08:49.394 --> 00:08:51.997
-When the President said the
Russian interference was a hoax,

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.133
that was false, wasn't it?
-True.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:57.670
-Now, compare that to how Trump
reacted just a few hours later.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:01.406
-There was no defense
to this ridiculous hoax,

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:07.012
this witch hunt that's been
going on for a long time.

00:09:07.012 --> 00:09:08.847
And everybody knew
it was a hoax.

00:09:08.847 --> 00:09:11.783
WikiLeaks is a hoax
just like everything else.

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:15.020
And all of those problems
having to do with crime

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.022
were the biggest hoax of all.

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:19.324
It was a witch hunt,
a total witch hunt.

00:09:19.324 --> 00:09:22.127
We did nothing wrong.
The answer's very simple.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:25.264
Nothing was done wrong.
This was all a big hoax.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.933
-Okay, I know
you watched the hearing,

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:30.469
but did you listen
or did your aides

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:32.071
secretly dub over
Mueller's lines

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.740
with Sean Hannity saying
nice things about you?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.376
-Hannity: The witch hunt
is officially over.

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.177
The Mueller Report is out,

00:09:39.177 --> 00:09:41.080
and the President
of the United States

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.517
has been totally
and completely vindicated.

00:09:45.517 --> 00:09:46.919
-The President and his allies

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:49.354
have immediately started lying
about yesterday's hearings

00:09:49.354 --> 00:09:52.058
because those hearings laid out
in clear and unequivocal terms

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:53.292
the story of what happened,

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:54.827
and that story
is incredibly damning.

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:57.162
At this point,
it's up to Congress
to do something about it.

00:09:57.162 --> 00:09:58.997
They could either stand by
and do nothing

00:09:58.997 --> 00:10:01.600
or they can impeach...
-Our president -- me.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.070
-This has been "A Closer Look."

